1
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:32,890
Boo!

2
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:36,760
There you are.

3
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:40,270
How did you start playing?

4
00:00:40,530 --> 00:00:41,440
So creepy.

5
00:00:46,940 --> 00:00:49,700
[Dobby, occupation: freelance host]

6
00:00:57,340 --> 00:00:59,560
Alright, babe, we can continue
where we left off!

7
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:01,490
"Babe," my ass!

8
00:01:01,510 --> 00:01:03,090
I'm on speakerphone.

9
00:01:03,110 --> 00:01:03,930
There are a lot of customers here.

10
00:01:03,950 --> 00:01:05,680
They might think I'm having an affair.

11
00:01:06,450 --> 00:01:08,120
It's my son, my son.

12
00:01:08,789 --> 00:01:11,000
Okay, I'll stop teasing you.

13
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:12,920
Let me give you an update.

14
00:01:12,940 --> 00:01:15,420
Tomorrow, there will be someone coming
to check out our dorm.

15
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,140
And if he likes it,

16
00:01:17,150 --> 00:01:18,000
he'll sign the contract.

17
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:19,800
If there's any update, I'll call you..

18
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:21,289
But most importantly,

19
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:22,940
you need to get plenty of rest.

20
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:23,840
Did you catch a cold?

21
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:24,890
Your voice is different.

22
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:25,910
Go to bed early.

23
00:01:25,930 --> 00:01:27,220
Then...

24
00:01:27,789 --> 00:01:29,110
I'll hang up now, babe!

25
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:30,930
Muah, muah!

26
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:33,650
Couldn't scold me in time, could you?
Go ahead!

27
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:35,360
Go ahead!

28
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:41,539
Huh?

29
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:43,220
There's a safe here?

30
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:47,370
What's the password?

31
00:01:48,270 --> 00:01:49,400
Is it his birthday?

32
00:01:53,289 --> 00:01:56,490
"Born on February 1, 1951."

33
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:57,870
Hey!

34
00:01:58,430 --> 00:01:59,670
Why did I suddenly get goosebumps?

35
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:12,280
Maybe I'm imagining things.

36
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,310
Why this brand, though?

37
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:33,940
Whoa...

38
00:02:33,970 --> 00:02:34,750
Whoa, whoa.

39
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,520
What's wrong with the lights?

40
00:02:37,270 --> 00:02:38,270
Whoa...

41
00:02:38,810 --> 00:02:39,520
Hey!

42
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:40,350
Hey!

43
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:42,870
Hey!!

44
00:02:43,160 --> 00:02:44,160
My flashlight.

45
00:02:45,510 --> 00:02:46,510
Where's the breaker?

46
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:51,200
Oh.

47
00:02:52,490 --> 00:02:53,820
Hey, hey.

48
00:03:14,710 --> 00:03:15,790
Come on!

49
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:17,560
Ow!

50
00:03:18,570 --> 00:03:19,340
Ouch...

51
00:03:21,100 --> 00:03:22,020
Aah, a ghost!

52
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:25,829
Namo Tassa Bhagavato
Arahato Sammā-Sambuddhassa!

53
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:28,550
Namo Tassa Bhagavato
Arahato Sammā-Sambuddhassa!

54
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,700
He's still here!

55
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,140
Chinese ghost.

56
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:32,990
Da cuo te cuo bu yao lai

57
00:03:33,010 --> 00:03:34,380
Wu ru wo de mei

58
00:03:34,430 --> 00:03:35,910
Po zhew lai zhe wa chai wa zho wa

59
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,150
Wo chai eur zhe zhe wo

60
00:03:38,230 --> 00:03:40,300
Da cuo te cuo bu yao lai

61
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,270
Well, I'm a Chinese girlie

62
00:03:49,290 --> 00:03:50,430
I didn't mean to

63
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:54,050
[Grandpa Danai, occupation: ghost]
[Previous owner of The D Dorm]

64
00:03:59,570 --> 00:04:02,650
[The D Dorm]

65
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:07,320
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

66
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:11,360
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

67
00:04:13,870 --> 00:04:19,310
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

68
00:04:21,029 --> 00:04:25,800
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

69
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:34,370
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

70
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:39,909
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

71
00:04:39,930 --> 00:04:43,440
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

72
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:47,040
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

73
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:50,580
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

74
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:53,240
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

75
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:59,580
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

76
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:06,690
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

77
00:05:07,170 --> 00:05:14,320
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

78
00:05:14,340 --> 00:05:21,400
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

79
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:25,360
[The D Dorm]

80
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:26,980
[The D Dorm]

81
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:30,590
Mr. Dobby,

82
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,480
are you alright?

83
00:05:31,630 --> 00:05:33,640
Mr. Dobby. Hello!

84
00:05:33,659 --> 00:05:35,290
Oh, hello, Mr. Somchai.

85
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:36,320
Sompong!

86
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:38,960
Oh, Mr. Sompong!

87
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:41,460
I didn't sleep very well last night.

88
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:42,960
I'll take you to

89
00:05:42,980 --> 00:05:44,980
every corner of this dorm.

90
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,440
May I have a moment?

91
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:47,970
- Yes.
- One second.

92
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:51,400
Dobby, wake up!

93
00:05:57,880 --> 00:05:58,880
Hello, Mr. Sompong.

94
00:05:58,909 --> 00:06:01,620
- Hello.
- I'll take you to every corner of this building.

95
00:06:01,640 --> 00:06:03,960
If you look at the area as a whole,

96
00:06:03,980 --> 00:06:05,350
it's like we have a male dragon

97
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:07,110
curled up right here.

98
00:06:07,310 --> 00:06:08,740
Starting from the north!

99
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:10,200
We have the dragon's head.

100
00:06:10,220 --> 00:06:10,810
The south!

101
00:06:11,310 --> 00:06:12,400
We have the dragon's tail.

102
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:14,160
And where we're standing!

103
00:06:14,480 --> 00:06:15,480
Right here.

104
00:06:15,610 --> 00:06:16,720
Is the dragon's junk!

105
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:17,540
That's right.

106
00:06:17,560 --> 00:06:18,220
Hey!

107
00:06:18,240 --> 00:06:19,120
Mr. Sompong!

108
00:06:19,130 --> 00:06:20,200
The dragon's junk is a bit too low.

109
00:06:20,220 --> 00:06:21,400
Its belly button is enough.

110
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:24,320
The dragon's belly button
is like when the dragon eats something

111
00:06:24,340 --> 00:06:26,520
and gets full,
once it's full, it's prosperous, right?

112
00:06:26,540 --> 00:06:28,640
So if you want to buy this place,

113
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:29,210
tear it down,

114
00:06:29,230 --> 00:06:31,440
and build a brand-new mall,

115
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:32,290
mark my words,

116
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:33,600
it's gonna flourish!

117
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:34,520
Flourish!

118
00:06:34,550 --> 00:06:37,100
And flourish, Mr. Sompong!

119
00:06:37,130 --> 00:06:38,270
I like the word "flourish."

120
00:06:38,280 --> 00:06:39,909
Then I'll go take another look around.

121
00:06:39,930 --> 00:06:41,030
Of course, Mr. Sompong.

122
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:42,670
The area on your left

123
00:06:42,690 --> 00:06:44,040
can be turned into a food court.

124
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,159
On the right...

125
00:06:45,180 --> 00:06:46,590
wow, if you tear it all down

126
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,659
and put in high-end brands,

127
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,000
it's going to be marvelous, Mr. Sompong.

128
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:51,720
I don't really mind the location.

129
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:53,360
- Yes.
- But I was wondering...

130
00:06:53,440 --> 00:06:55,159
the previous owner of this dorm,

131
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,590
he, uh...

132
00:06:58,980 --> 00:06:59,800
passed away right here.

133
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,760
Seriously, are there ghosts here?

134
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:07,910
No way!

135
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:09,390
There definitely aren't any here.

136
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:12,960
I've lived here and never seen one.

137
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:13,840
Okay.

138
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,920
Grandpa!

139
00:07:28,560 --> 00:07:30,920
Hey, what are you so scared of?!
[Rooms For Rent, Welcome]

140
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:35,480
[Danis, occupation: manager of The D Dorm]

141
00:07:38,190 --> 00:07:38,659
Oh!

142
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:40,620
I'm sorry, Mr. Sompong.

143
00:07:40,990 --> 00:07:41,880
What's wrong with you?!

144
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,110
Why did you bring out
a dead person's photo?!

145
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:44,540
It's just a sign, isn't it?

146
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:46,720
I put it at the front
and call customers every day!

147
00:07:47,840 --> 00:07:49,560
Hello.

148
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:51,480
Are you here to rent a room?

149
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:54,620
I'm Danis, the manager of this dorm.

150
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,920
Welcome.

151
00:07:56,940 --> 00:07:58,880
I'm not renting.
I want to buy this building.

152
00:07:58,970 --> 00:08:00,760
Then, by all means, get out of here!

153
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,480
We're not selling it!

154
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:03,320
Hey!

155
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:05,130
How could you say that to my customer?!

156
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:06,700
Mr. Sompong, I'll be back soon.

157
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:07,310
Give me a moment.

158
00:08:07,330 --> 00:08:07,970
Hey, you!

159
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,080
Come talk to me first!

160
00:08:09,590 --> 00:08:10,140
Hey!

161
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:11,270
Stay here, alright, Gramps?

162
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:12,470
- What?!
- You.

163
00:08:12,500 --> 00:08:14,300
How could you chase
my customers away like that?!

164
00:08:14,310 --> 00:08:16,160
Whether we sell it or not
is up to his descendants,

165
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:16,800
not you!

166
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:19,160
If Gramps had a choice,
he wouldn't leave the dorm to you!

167
00:08:19,970 --> 00:08:20,980
And all this time,

168
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,200
how come you never
took care of your Grandpa?

169
00:08:23,270 --> 00:08:24,920
You left him all alone.

170
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:25,890
How could you do that?!

171
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:26,980
Do you even care?!

172
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:28,710
He just passed away,

173
00:08:28,730 --> 00:08:29,990
and you're selling his property?

174
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:30,730
Are you crazy?!

175
00:08:30,750 --> 00:08:31,960
He loved this dorm!

176
00:08:35,070 --> 00:08:35,990
I'm gonna pass out...

177
00:08:37,010 --> 00:08:38,010
Are you alright, Miss?

178
00:08:38,370 --> 00:08:39,590
That's refreshing... I'll continue.

179
00:08:39,610 --> 00:08:40,990
You're shameless, outrageous,

180
00:08:41,010 --> 00:08:42,000
brazen, greedy!

181
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:42,730
Enough!

182
00:08:42,750 --> 00:08:43,780
You're about to say "awful," aren't you?

183
00:08:43,799 --> 00:08:44,520
Huh, how did you know?

184
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:45,380
You're dissing me

185
00:08:45,400 --> 00:08:46,850
with this much passion,
of course I'd know!

186
00:08:46,860 --> 00:08:47,970
Do you breathe through your gills?

187
00:08:47,990 --> 00:08:49,530
Where I breathe from
is none of your business,

188
00:08:49,550 --> 00:08:51,040
but I won't let this place be sold.

189
00:08:51,130 --> 00:08:53,740
Do you know how much
Gramps loved this place?!

190
00:08:53,760 --> 00:08:55,340
Right, Gramps?

191
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,310
It doesn't matter how much
he loved this dorm!

192
00:08:57,330 --> 00:08:58,400
It's mine now,

193
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,920
and I'll sell it!

194
00:09:02,030 --> 00:09:03,400
Gramps! Gramps, did you hear that?

195
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:04,760
If you don't want this dorm sold...

196
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:05,650
Tonight,

197
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:08,180
come break your ungrateful
grandson's neck!

198
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:09,400
Sadhu, sadhu!

199
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,710
Put him away!

200
00:09:19,030 --> 00:09:20,640
Not here.
Mr. Sompong might misunderstand!

201
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:23,220
Gramps, you can hear me, right?

202
00:09:25,610 --> 00:09:27,000
- Uh, Mr. Dobby?
- Yes?

203
00:09:27,120 --> 00:09:30,550
I'll have to bring a Feng Shui Master
to check this place again.

204
00:09:30,630 --> 00:09:33,280
My boss takes this very seriously.

205
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:37,080
- Uh...
- If we buy a place with a territorial ghost,

206
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:39,570
- nothing will prosper there.
- Right.

207
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:40,400
I'll come back later.

208
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:41,760
- Why not now?
- Don't touch me.

209
00:09:41,780 --> 00:09:43,550
- Mr. Sompong, please!
- I don't believe it!

210
00:09:43,570 --> 00:09:44,480
I'm not listening.

211
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:45,970
- See you later.
- Mr. Sompong, there are no ghosts here.

212
00:09:45,990 --> 00:09:46,810
- Stop it.
- Mr. Sompong.

213
00:09:48,010 --> 00:09:49,450
You...

214
00:09:49,550 --> 00:09:50,640
Are you a house gecko or something?

215
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:54,020
- Gramps!
- Come on!

216
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:55,000
Mr. Sompong.

217
00:09:57,690 --> 00:09:59,200
Hey! Take this with you!

218
00:09:59,920 --> 00:10:02,050
[Duangjai's Kitchen, Made-to-Order Food]

219
00:10:05,930 --> 00:10:06,930
Aunite, Auntie.

220
00:10:07,010 --> 00:10:08,610
- Yeah?
- Here's your cooking gas.

221
00:10:08,820 --> 00:10:10,230
Where's the old tank?

222
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:11,180
Here.

223
00:10:13,870 --> 00:10:14,650
Hey!

224
00:10:17,370 --> 00:10:20,090
[Auntie Duang, occupation: restaurant owner]

225
00:10:20,210 --> 00:10:21,670
I'm not a gas tank!

226
00:10:21,690 --> 00:10:22,650
Are you crazy?

227
00:10:22,670 --> 00:10:24,980
- Then where is it?
- Over there, at the back!

228
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:26,930
Here.

229
00:10:26,950 --> 00:10:29,090
I saw something short and green,
so I thought you were a gas tank.

230
00:10:29,110 --> 00:10:30,690
Green is an auspicious color.

231
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:31,940
It helps bring in money, you know?

232
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:34,090
Wow, short? Sadhu,

233
00:10:34,110 --> 00:10:36,030
I hope your wife is as short as I am!

234
00:10:37,530 --> 00:10:39,160
Oh, Danis! What are you having?

235
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:40,480
I don't feel like eating, Auntie.

236
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:41,690
I'm mad at Gramps' grandson.

237
00:10:41,710 --> 00:10:43,160
He plans to sell this building.

238
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:45,000
He brought someone
to look at our dorm today, too!

239
00:10:45,020 --> 00:10:45,740
Mr. Sompong?

240
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:48,140
Oh? You know him, too?

241
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:49,750
A little, yeah.

242
00:10:49,770 --> 00:10:51,910
Mr. Sompong used to work in
the procurement department.

243
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:53,190
He's looking for a spot to build a mall.

244
00:10:53,200 --> 00:10:54,300
Most importantly,

245
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,760
he's single right now!

246
00:10:55,790 --> 00:10:57,070
He loves pad kra pao

247
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:58,450
with a runny fried egg. It's his favorite.

248
00:10:58,470 --> 00:11:00,450
But he's not that fun to talk to,
he's quite serious.

249
00:11:00,550 --> 00:11:03,370
Wow! And you say
you only know him a little?

250
00:11:03,410 --> 00:11:04,880
Well...

251
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:07,250
Well, my mom knows everything.

252
00:11:07,330 --> 00:11:08,770
The only thing she doesn't know

253
00:11:08,790 --> 00:11:10,290
is where her husband has gone.

254
00:11:10,620 --> 00:11:12,140
Oh, wow!

255
00:11:12,150 --> 00:11:15,220
I hear your voice, but where are you?

256
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:17,010
I'm here!

257
00:11:20,970 --> 00:11:23,770
[Dolly, occupation: stylist]
[Auntie Duang's youngest son]

258
00:11:25,910 --> 00:11:27,170
Hello, Mom.

259
00:11:27,290 --> 00:11:28,520
I almost had a heart attack.

260
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:30,050
You're a grown-up now,
don't mess around like a kid.

261
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:31,640
And what are you doing with my curtain?

262
00:11:31,660 --> 00:11:32,820
I'll borrow it for now, Mom.

263
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:34,820
Look, the pattern is nice.

264
00:11:34,850 --> 00:11:37,250
I still can't find a red-carpet dress
for my customer.

265
00:11:37,270 --> 00:11:38,240
Stop right there.

266
00:11:39,170 --> 00:11:41,310
Your customer's swimsuit is still here.

267
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:45,370
Oh, come on now, Mom.

268
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:47,450
They're going to
sell the dorm anyway, aren't they?

269
00:11:47,470 --> 00:11:50,010
I'll buy you new ones
after we finish moving, alright?

270
00:11:50,030 --> 00:11:51,570
No, we're not moving.

271
00:11:51,940 --> 00:11:53,380
A building in a prime location like this

272
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:54,660
is very hard to find nowadays.

273
00:11:54,680 --> 00:11:56,260
And it's good that I'm here

274
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:57,880
cause it's near
where your brother is stationed.

275
00:12:09,370 --> 00:12:12,010
[Dollar, occupation: community relations officer]
[Auntie Duang's oldest son]

276
00:12:21,050 --> 00:12:22,250
Dollar, dear,

277
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:23,610
what happened to your leg?

278
00:12:23,710 --> 00:12:25,890
Well, you made me
pad see ew this morning,

279
00:12:25,910 --> 00:12:27,330
so I ran to burn it off.

280
00:12:27,410 --> 00:12:28,930
There's no need for that.

281
00:12:29,110 --> 00:12:30,180
Hey!

282
00:12:30,190 --> 00:12:32,000
You were so cute with that chubby,

283
00:12:32,010 --> 00:12:33,340
cuddly belly you used to have!

284
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,060
It's not lunch break yet.

285
00:12:37,080 --> 00:12:37,770
Why are you here?

286
00:12:37,790 --> 00:12:39,220
Dolly called me and said

287
00:12:39,310 --> 00:12:40,500
we have to close the shop and move.

288
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:42,900
Is that true?

289
00:12:44,090 --> 00:12:45,520
No one will have to move away!

290
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:47,370
I'll protect Gramps' dorm.

291
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:48,840
I won't allow anyone

292
00:12:48,850 --> 00:12:50,160
to sell this building!

293
00:12:51,090 --> 00:12:51,840
Splendid!

294
00:12:51,860 --> 00:12:53,100
Let me know if you need help.

295
00:12:53,260 --> 00:12:55,500
I'll also help you protect this dorm.

296
00:12:56,450 --> 00:12:57,520
Me too, Mom!

297
00:12:59,630 --> 00:13:00,520
Dollar.

298
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:04,560
Whatever you and Dolly say,

299
00:13:04,580 --> 00:13:05,760
I'm with you.

300
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:06,910
No,

301
00:13:07,470 --> 00:13:08,770
I want you to help me change the gas tank.

302
00:13:09,860 --> 00:13:10,600
Ugh...

303
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:16,860
What's wrong?

304
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:17,880
The weight is just right.

305
00:13:18,730 --> 00:13:19,820
Can I do one set?

306
00:13:22,680 --> 00:13:23,260
Mm, alright.

307
00:13:24,850 --> 00:13:25,930
Oh, wow...

308
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:28,010
Mom, wanna try?

309
00:13:28,030 --> 00:13:28,680
No, thanks!

310
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:35,900
I said I'm going to sell this building!

311
00:13:35,930 --> 00:13:38,090
Why does she need to put this sign here?

312
00:13:38,240 --> 00:13:38,980
You, too.

313
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:39,760
Why?
[Rooms For Rent, Welcome]

314
00:13:39,810 --> 00:13:40,810
You love this building that much?

315
00:13:40,830 --> 00:13:43,010
Is that why you keep
haunting your descendants?

316
00:13:43,150 --> 00:13:44,530
I've already called an exorcist here.

317
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:45,670
Just you wait,

318
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,010
and we'll see who prevails.

319
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:52,840
Hey.

320
00:13:56,590 --> 00:13:58,290
For yin and yang to stay balanced,

321
00:13:58,580 --> 00:14:00,450
humans and ghosts must
not cross paths.

322
00:14:00,490 --> 00:14:02,490
Yin and yang have their flow,

323
00:14:02,510 --> 00:14:03,830
humans and ghosts

324
00:14:03,850 --> 00:14:05,290
must not...

325
00:14:05,310 --> 00:14:06,800
share the same realm!

326
00:14:07,820 --> 00:14:08,880
What are you...

327
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:10,550
- even doing, huh?!
- Ow!

328
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:11,420
What the heck, Dobby?

329
00:14:11,430 --> 00:14:12,040
It hurts, you know?

330
00:14:12,290 --> 00:14:15,090
[Dax, occupation: supporting actor]

331
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:15,770
What are you doing?

332
00:14:15,790 --> 00:14:18,290
Weren't you looking for an exorcist
to drive away your grandpa's ghost?

333
00:14:18,380 --> 00:14:18,740
Mm.

334
00:14:18,760 --> 00:14:21,120
Well, that is me!

335
00:14:21,130 --> 00:14:22,350
I was looking for an exorcist,

336
00:14:22,930 --> 00:14:24,320
not a supporting actor.

337
00:14:27,490 --> 00:14:29,010
It's called a supporting role.

338
00:14:29,170 --> 00:14:30,290
- Most importantly,
- Mm.

339
00:14:30,380 --> 00:14:31,170
I have

340
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,830
been cast as an exorcist
in a Chinese series.

341
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,840
- Which one?
- 'Khemjira: The Kowloon Necropolis Edition.'

342
00:14:36,910 --> 00:14:38,950
The one who showed up for
three seconds before getting killed?

343
00:14:38,980 --> 00:14:39,650
That doesn't count.

344
00:14:42,550 --> 00:14:44,190
Don't you belittle the art of acting.

345
00:14:44,210 --> 00:14:45,370
Although I only appeared for three seconds...

346
00:14:45,470 --> 00:14:46,810
to really get into the role,

347
00:14:46,830 --> 00:14:49,170
I even took an exorcism course.

348
00:14:49,290 --> 00:14:50,200
I got a certificate.

349
00:14:50,210 --> 00:14:51,170
Oh, you got one?!

350
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,310
Here.

351
00:14:52,340 --> 00:14:54,130
Ow! Your certificate is very hard.

352
00:14:54,150 --> 00:14:55,160
- Here, see this?
- Back up a little.

353
00:14:55,170 --> 00:14:55,650
Look.

354
00:14:56,130 --> 00:14:57,240
Whoa, it's real?

355
00:14:57,620 --> 00:14:58,530
You're something else, man.

356
00:14:58,560 --> 00:14:59,190
That's right.

357
00:14:59,200 --> 00:15:00,320
So,

358
00:15:00,340 --> 00:15:01,520
don't you worry.

359
00:15:01,540 --> 00:15:02,210
Today,

360
00:15:02,220 --> 00:15:04,480
I'll perform a ritual
to send your grandpa's ghost

361
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:06,530
straight back to Shantou!

362
00:15:06,550 --> 00:15:08,540
Good, look at his face there.

363
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:09,360
He haunts me every night.

364
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:10,970
I can't get any sleep.

365
00:15:13,780 --> 00:15:15,460
Gramps' ghost?

366
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:17,760
Is Dobby so deathly afraid of ghosts

367
00:15:17,780 --> 00:15:19,570
that he had to call an exorcist?

368
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:28,140
♫I can only say I love you so much♫

369
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:31,950
♫Love you so much♫

370
00:15:31,970 --> 00:15:38,010
♫There's no measure for this love of mine♫

371
00:15:41,890 --> 00:15:44,530
[Daeng the Handyman,
occupation: dorm handyman]

372
00:15:49,290 --> 00:15:50,450
Aren't I cool?

373
00:15:50,470 --> 00:15:51,570
Cool?

374
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:53,230
My documents are all over the place.

375
00:15:53,250 --> 00:15:54,440
Oh! I'm sorry.

376
00:15:54,460 --> 00:15:55,370
Let me pick them up for you.

377
00:15:55,390 --> 00:15:56,260
Leave them for now.

378
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:58,090
I need your help. It's urgent.

379
00:15:58,110 --> 00:15:59,160
You know, right?

380
00:15:59,180 --> 00:16:00,130
Gramps' grandson

381
00:16:00,150 --> 00:16:01,490
is going to sell this place!

382
00:16:01,510 --> 00:16:02,160
Huh?!

383
00:16:02,340 --> 00:16:03,560
Daeng, help me think of

384
00:16:03,570 --> 00:16:05,520
a way to stop Gramps' grandson.

385
00:16:05,780 --> 00:16:07,060
Mm...

386
00:16:07,070 --> 00:16:08,270
Why don't we...

387
00:16:09,210 --> 00:16:10,470
just tell him directly?

388
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:12,340
That we...

389
00:16:12,370 --> 00:16:13,270
love this place

390
00:16:13,290 --> 00:16:14,870
and are very attached to it.

391
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:17,370
Maybe our sincerity

392
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:18,890
will reach him,

393
00:16:19,450 --> 00:16:21,200
and we might be able to change his mind!

394
00:16:22,730 --> 00:16:24,970
Ugh! Daeng, there you go
being optimistic again.

395
00:16:25,310 --> 00:16:26,270
Someone like him

396
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:27,800
wouldn't care about our feelings.

397
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:30,720
You need a dirty plan

398
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:32,730
to deal with a dirty person.

399
00:16:33,110 --> 00:16:34,230
Uh...

400
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,450
I don't think dirty things are my forte.
Unlike you.

401
00:16:40,530 --> 00:16:41,850
I think

402
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:43,220
you'd be better off

403
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,060
consulting my twin brother

404
00:16:45,530 --> 00:16:46,770
about this.

405
00:16:46,870 --> 00:16:47,770
Dum the Guard?

406
00:16:48,890 --> 00:16:50,330
I know it's fitting,

407
00:16:50,340 --> 00:16:52,850
but Dum? Can he really
come up with a dirty plan?

408
00:16:54,490 --> 00:16:57,010
♫I love you more than anyone♫

409
00:16:57,050 --> 00:17:00,200
♫I give my heart to you, my dearest one♫

410
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:03,170
[Dum the Guard,
occupation: dorm security guard]

411
00:17:03,250 --> 00:17:04,310
That's enough, Dum.

412
00:17:04,319 --> 00:17:05,579
If you don't stop singing,

413
00:17:05,589 --> 00:17:06,829
you're going to lose your job.

414
00:17:06,849 --> 00:17:07,839
Oh...roger that!

415
00:17:07,990 --> 00:17:08,839
I won't sing anymore.

416
00:17:08,859 --> 00:17:11,300
Seriously, are you two really twins?

417
00:17:11,410 --> 00:17:12,619
Your parents didn't adopt one of you

418
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,810
and say that to make you feel better, right?

419
00:17:13,829 --> 00:17:15,339
Don't say that, Ms. Danis!

420
00:17:15,410 --> 00:17:16,099
Why?

421
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:18,970
Although we look different,

422
00:17:18,990 --> 00:17:20,930
we each have our own charm.

423
00:17:21,050 --> 00:17:22,170
Look at this,

424
00:17:22,210 --> 00:17:23,960
eyes that resemble an eagle's,

425
00:17:24,730 --> 00:17:26,760
a nose that resembles a lion's.

426
00:17:26,859 --> 00:17:28,810
Those lips are definitely a wild gaur's.

427
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:30,170
Legs that resemble
a Sumatran rhinoceros's.

428
00:17:30,570 --> 00:17:31,920
Ears as grand as an elephant's,

429
00:17:32,230 --> 00:17:36,560
with a tummy as plump
as Po's from Kung Fu Panda!

430
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:37,770
That's enough.

431
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:39,650
The more you present me,
the less human I become.

432
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:40,380
What was that?

433
00:17:40,390 --> 00:17:42,060
I'm a security guard,
not an ambassador for Safari World.

434
00:17:42,090 --> 00:17:43,380
You only mentioned animals.

435
00:17:43,780 --> 00:17:44,580
But...

436
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,990
you're cute to me.

437
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:49,360
Po!

438
00:17:49,370 --> 00:17:50,890
Do you want some steamed buns?

439
00:17:50,990 --> 00:17:52,500
Ugh! Now that you're here,

440
00:17:52,510 --> 00:17:53,570
help me figure out

441
00:17:53,600 --> 00:17:55,480
how to stop Gramps' grandson

442
00:17:55,500 --> 00:17:57,130
from selling this dorm.

443
00:17:57,310 --> 00:17:58,260
Mm...

444
00:17:58,270 --> 00:17:59,690
I might have a plan.

445
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:00,900
And that is?

446
00:18:03,210 --> 00:18:05,680
[The D Dorm]

447
00:18:10,490 --> 00:18:11,730
Hey, he might already be here!

448
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:18,690
Dobby.

449
00:18:18,730 --> 00:18:19,400
Hm?

450
00:18:19,410 --> 00:18:20,210
Stop messing around.

451
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:22,290
I'm not. You were tapping in rhythm.

452
00:18:22,630 --> 00:18:24,210
It's serious. Sorry.

453
00:18:31,570 --> 00:18:33,860
Great Gods of Heaven and Earth,

454
00:18:34,550 --> 00:18:36,890
celestial generals
and commanders of the five directions,

455
00:18:37,970 --> 00:18:40,230
sacred armies and heavenly steeds...

456
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:41,440
Here it comes.

457
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:43,800
Sacred armies and heavenly steeds...

458
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:46,410
Pass me the sword.

459
00:18:48,010 --> 00:18:49,190
Oh, you're talking to me?

460
00:18:52,570 --> 00:18:55,230
Pasme de talisman.

461
00:18:55,250 --> 00:18:56,750
Here it is again!

462
00:18:56,870 --> 00:18:59,170
Pasme de talisman.

463
00:19:01,810 --> 00:19:03,030
Pass me the talisman.

464
00:19:03,230 --> 00:19:04,290
Come on...

465
00:19:04,300 --> 00:19:05,160
Why did you say that with an accent?

466
00:19:08,490 --> 00:19:09,760
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

467
00:19:13,780 --> 00:19:14,620
Ow! Whoa.

468
00:19:14,630 --> 00:19:16,480
- Hold your sword properly.
- Oh...

469
00:19:17,190 --> 00:19:18,430
- Sorry, sorry.
- Dax.

470
00:19:21,250 --> 00:19:24,430
Grandpa's spirit, reveal yourself!

471
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:27,470
Grandpa's spirit, reveal yourself!

472
00:19:27,970 --> 00:19:30,350
Grandpa's spirit, reveal yourself!

473
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:33,730
Grandpa's spirit, reveal yourself!

474
00:19:34,210 --> 00:19:36,610
Grandpa's spirit, reveal yourself!

475
00:19:37,390 --> 00:19:38,630
Dax, quit messing around!

476
00:19:38,650 --> 00:19:40,050
Stop tickling me, then!

477
00:19:40,070 --> 00:19:41,320
Okay, okay, sorry.

478
00:19:41,550 --> 00:19:44,290
Grandpa's spirit, reveal yourself!

479
00:19:44,310 --> 00:19:45,990
Reveal yourself!

480
00:19:46,010 --> 00:19:47,990
Reveal yourself!

481
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:51,050
Who dares summon me?!

482
00:19:59,770 --> 00:20:01,330
Dax, do you see that?

483
00:20:01,350 --> 00:20:02,310
Grandpa's ghost!

484
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,640
I see him, I see him.

485
00:20:08,890 --> 00:20:10,200
You ungrateful grandson.

486
00:20:11,090 --> 00:20:12,930
Not only do you plan to sell my dorm,

487
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,420
but you also called
an exorcist to challenge me?

488
00:20:15,800 --> 00:20:16,940
Grandpa!

489
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:18,490
You're the one who started this!

490
00:20:19,210 --> 00:20:20,780
Ghosts should stay with ghosts!

491
00:20:20,800 --> 00:20:22,610
- That's right.
- Why are you bothering me?!

492
00:20:22,630 --> 00:20:24,510
But this is my property!

493
00:20:24,530 --> 00:20:25,710
If you still plan to sell it,

494
00:20:25,740 --> 00:20:26,850
I'll break your neck!

495
00:20:26,870 --> 00:20:27,770
How is it yours?!

496
00:20:28,350 --> 00:20:29,550
It's Mom's now!

497
00:20:31,120 --> 00:20:32,090
- Dax.
- What?

498
00:20:32,110 --> 00:20:33,360
Banish him already!

499
00:20:35,140 --> 00:20:35,950
Shoo...

500
00:20:36,290 --> 00:20:36,970
Shoo...

501
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:37,630
Go.

502
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:38,600
Go away!

503
00:20:38,620 --> 00:20:40,160
Go. Shoo.

504
00:20:40,170 --> 00:20:40,740
Hey!

505
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:42,890
You're shooing a dog, not a ghost.

506
00:20:42,910 --> 00:20:44,130
Shooing a ghost, not a dog.

507
00:20:45,170 --> 00:20:47,060
Dax, didn't you say you studied exorcism?

508
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,450
Do something!

509
00:20:48,890 --> 00:20:49,920
Oh...okay.

510
00:20:51,070 --> 00:20:52,080
Throw it.

511
00:20:52,530 --> 00:20:53,370
Throw it. Do it.

512
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:54,300
Throw it already. Throw...

513
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:54,690
Hey!

514
00:20:54,970 --> 00:20:56,770
- Stop shivering already. Just throw it.
- Okay.

515
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:07,570
Hey, wait.

516
00:21:08,970 --> 00:21:09,690
Hey!

517
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,760
Keep throwing, you losers.

518
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:14,120
You're not going to hit me anyway.

519
00:21:15,370 --> 00:21:16,000
Stop.

520
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:16,410
Let me.

521
00:21:16,850 --> 00:21:18,110
You think you're so tough, huh?

522
00:21:21,290 --> 00:21:21,710
See that?

523
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:23,010
How can a ghost get winded?

524
00:21:23,970 --> 00:21:24,980
Come to think of it...

525
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:26,550
he wasn't this bloated

526
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:27,980
the last time I saw him.

527
00:21:28,290 --> 00:21:29,350
Did he drown?

528
00:21:30,280 --> 00:21:31,250
He died on the stairs.

529
00:21:31,750 --> 00:21:33,210
Is he gonna be alright?

530
00:21:33,470 --> 00:21:34,330
No?

531
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:35,760
That probably hurt.

532
00:21:36,200 --> 00:21:36,760
Give that to me.

533
00:21:37,920 --> 00:21:38,790
- Dobby.
- Huh?

534
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:39,810
What are you gonna do?

535
00:21:40,410 --> 00:21:41,680
I want to get a closer look.

536
00:21:42,030 --> 00:21:42,800
Let's see.

537
00:21:42,820 --> 00:21:44,660
If this isn't Grandpa's ghost,
I'll beat you until you're skinny.

538
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:49,030
- I'm screwed!
- Grandpa...

539
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:51,640
Hey, Dobby, my beloved grandson.

540
00:21:52,260 --> 00:21:53,210
It is

541
00:21:53,230 --> 00:21:55,510
getting late, so I should get some sleep.

542
00:21:55,530 --> 00:21:58,330
I have an errand early tomorrow morning.

543
00:21:58,450 --> 00:22:01,410
Don't sell this dorm yet.
I'll be back soon.

544
00:22:01,430 --> 00:22:02,980
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

545
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:03,910
Where are you going?!

546
00:22:11,210 --> 00:22:13,390
Dum, quick! Run!

547
00:22:13,410 --> 00:22:14,520
Go! Hurry!

548
00:22:14,540 --> 00:22:16,330
There's a whole gang here!
Hurry, get them!

549
00:22:18,450 --> 00:22:19,500
Hey, where did they go?

550
00:22:22,290 --> 00:22:23,550
Hey! Where are you going?!

551
00:22:42,200 --> 00:22:44,200
Oh, wow...

552
00:22:44,270 --> 00:22:46,480
- Wait...
- Jeez, you just keep poking me.

553
00:22:47,770 --> 00:22:49,170
This is Grandpa,

554
00:22:49,180 --> 00:22:50,930
not a dead dog.

555
00:22:55,250 --> 00:22:56,370
Grandpa!

556
00:22:56,990 --> 00:22:57,850
Grandpa's ghost...

557
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:09,300
My beloved grandson, you poor thing.

558
00:23:09,690 --> 00:23:11,010
Dobby!

559
00:23:11,030 --> 00:23:11,990
Stay away, Grandpa!

560
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:14,050
Where are you going?

561
00:23:14,070 --> 00:23:15,070
Don't follow me!

562
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:20,400
Why the hell can't I open it?

563
00:23:24,520 --> 00:23:26,720
That is not a doorknob.

564
00:23:27,220 --> 00:23:28,180
Grandpa!

565
00:23:28,210 --> 00:23:30,800
That is my knob...

566
00:23:33,450 --> 00:23:34,940
- Stay away.
- Where are you going?

567
00:23:34,950 --> 00:23:36,520
Why are you running away from me?

568
00:23:36,530 --> 00:23:38,630
- Stay away, Grandpa! I said stay away!
- Let us talk first.

569
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:39,770
Stop! Stop!

570
00:23:40,900 --> 00:23:42,090
Dobby.

571
00:23:42,110 --> 00:23:43,610
Oh, ghosts should fear talismans.

572
00:23:45,180 --> 00:23:45,710
Take this!

573
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:46,570
What?

574
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:50,300
You did not know?

575
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:52,940
These are all fake talismans.

576
00:23:54,000 --> 00:23:55,470
Here, look at this one.

577
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:57,470
What does it say?

578
00:23:57,690 --> 00:23:59,880
"I'm too rich. I can't take it anymore."

579
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:03,170
Maybe whoever wrote this
is a fan of Prime Minister Noo.

580
00:24:03,690 --> 00:24:04,650
You watch the news.

581
00:24:04,670 --> 00:24:06,480
- Talk to me.
- No!

582
00:24:06,510 --> 00:24:08,190
- I need to talk to you.
- No...don't come any closer.

583
00:24:08,210 --> 00:24:09,330
Don't come any closer.

584
00:24:09,350 --> 00:24:10,370
- Stay away.
- Dobby.

585
00:24:14,570 --> 00:24:16,570
Dobby!

586
00:24:16,980 --> 00:24:17,920
Dobby!

587
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:19,400
Dobby!

588
00:24:19,490 --> 00:24:20,920
Dobby!

589
00:24:21,050 --> 00:24:22,560
Dobby!

590
00:24:23,300 --> 00:24:24,160
Oh, I forgot.

591
00:24:24,170 --> 00:24:26,120
No matter how many times I try,
it does not work.

592
00:24:26,210 --> 00:24:27,860
I cannot touch him.

593
00:24:29,430 --> 00:24:31,810
But Heaven still has mercy on me,

594
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:34,330
allowing me to communicate with you.

595
00:24:34,370 --> 00:24:35,690
We get to see each other.

596
00:24:35,820 --> 00:24:37,120
Let us talk

597
00:24:37,140 --> 00:24:38,210
when you wake up,

598
00:24:38,230 --> 00:24:41,300
my beloved grandson.

599
00:24:42,170 --> 00:24:43,300
Muah, muah.

600
00:24:48,240 --> 00:24:49,650
[The D Dorm]

601
00:24:49,670 --> 00:24:51,810
[Duangjai's Kitchen, Made-to-Order Food]

602
00:24:55,540 --> 00:24:57,090
See how that went?

603
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,960
You dressed up as a ghost to trick him,

604
00:24:59,250 --> 00:25:00,620
but it almost got you sent to jail.

605
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:03,260
Luckily, Dollar is tight with
the duty officer.

606
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:05,090
So we were able to settle things
with that Dax guy.

607
00:25:05,260 --> 00:25:06,950
So this is the perk
of having a cop son, huh?

608
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:09,180
I can rest easy.
He's someone I can count on.

609
00:25:09,930 --> 00:25:12,050
Okay, everyone, dance with me!

610
00:25:14,010 --> 00:25:14,690
Come.

611
00:25:18,610 --> 00:25:20,040
Come on, move with me.

612
00:25:23,330 --> 00:25:24,130
Come on.

613
00:25:28,600 --> 00:25:31,210
He happens to lead
the community aerobics class.

614
00:25:31,310 --> 00:25:32,580
The police catch thieves for a living,

615
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:33,530
but your son

616
00:25:33,540 --> 00:25:34,570
can only catch the beat.

617
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:38,090
- One, two, three, four.
- What? Are you mocking me?

618
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:40,090
You'll have to exercise with me.

619
00:25:40,110 --> 00:25:41,240
Your muscles are all saggy now.

620
00:25:41,630 --> 00:25:43,250
- Mom!
- Don't be stubborn. Come here!

621
00:25:43,270 --> 00:25:44,070
- Mom!
- Go!

622
00:25:44,090 --> 00:25:45,680
But isn't it odd?

623
00:25:45,700 --> 00:25:48,430
Why didn't Dobby
come after us last night?

624
00:25:48,590 --> 00:25:49,710
Could it be that

625
00:25:50,370 --> 00:25:53,330
my little brother's cuteness and chubbiness

626
00:25:53,610 --> 00:25:54,780
made his anger go away?

627
00:25:56,210 --> 00:25:57,410
- No way!
- No way!

628
00:25:58,650 --> 00:26:00,470
Next time, don't mention my name
unless necessary.

629
00:26:00,990 --> 00:26:01,750
Like I got called in to get scolded.

630
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:02,180
See?

631
00:26:03,110 --> 00:26:04,400
What do you like about me so much?

632
00:26:04,620 --> 00:26:05,760
Mm...

633
00:26:06,180 --> 00:26:07,700
I don't feel good about this.

634
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:09,580
Should we...

635
00:26:10,290 --> 00:26:11,850
go get our fortune told?

636
00:26:12,450 --> 00:26:13,730
All of us.

637
00:26:14,270 --> 00:26:15,930
- Let's go, yeah?
- Go get our fortune read?

638
00:26:15,950 --> 00:26:16,810
Go take a shower.

639
00:26:17,490 --> 00:26:19,690
Hey, looking like this,
how could I not shower?

640
00:26:19,780 --> 00:26:21,580
The face paint's about to seep
into my epidermis.

641
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:22,890
No need for that.

642
00:26:23,290 --> 00:26:25,110
You don't have to shower.
Your skin might get dry.

643
00:26:25,130 --> 00:26:27,500
It's time for work. Your shift has started.

644
00:26:27,510 --> 00:26:27,890
Yeah.

645
00:26:27,900 --> 00:26:28,800
What thief would be scared of me

646
00:26:28,820 --> 00:26:29,400
looking like this?

647
00:26:30,190 --> 00:26:31,290
Let me take a shower.

648
00:26:33,370 --> 00:26:35,370
[D409]

649
00:26:57,720 --> 00:26:58,330
Hey!

650
00:26:59,070 --> 00:27:00,140
Why did you have to sit in the dark?

651
00:27:00,700 --> 00:27:01,800
The light works just fine.

652
00:27:02,060 --> 00:27:03,320
The light works just fine!

653
00:27:03,360 --> 00:27:05,060
The person who turned it on doesn't.

654
00:27:05,330 --> 00:27:07,290
What if our eyes can't adjust in time?!

655
00:27:07,930 --> 00:27:10,650
[Dawin, occupation: tarot reader]

656
00:27:10,730 --> 00:27:12,110
You might make me go blind!

657
00:27:12,150 --> 00:27:14,580
I'm turning on the light, not the sun!

658
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:15,810
Don't be so dramatic!!

659
00:27:16,730 --> 00:27:17,730
Hey!

660
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:19,890
Will there ever be a day

661
00:27:19,930 --> 00:27:21,460
when you two meet without arguing?

662
00:27:21,500 --> 00:27:22,840
Let's continue. Sit down!

663
00:27:23,070 --> 00:27:25,420
- Continue.
- Look at our cards first.

664
00:27:39,830 --> 00:27:40,900
Ten of Swords.

665
00:27:41,380 --> 00:27:43,600
It means that this dorm

666
00:27:43,750 --> 00:27:45,290
has come to an end.

667
00:27:45,360 --> 00:27:46,290
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

668
00:27:48,950 --> 00:27:50,170
The Tower.

669
00:27:50,790 --> 00:27:53,140
It signifies a sudden change!

670
00:27:56,010 --> 00:27:57,360
As for the Ten of Pentacles,

671
00:27:57,960 --> 00:28:00,250
it guarantees a sale.

672
00:28:02,730 --> 00:28:03,710
Are you implying that

673
00:28:03,730 --> 00:28:06,300
Dobby will sell this dorm
no matter what happens?

674
00:28:06,990 --> 00:28:07,720
So...

675
00:28:07,740 --> 00:28:08,660
is there any other way

676
00:28:08,680 --> 00:28:10,890
to save this dorm, Dawin?

677
00:28:11,230 --> 00:28:12,490
Draw one more card.

678
00:28:15,130 --> 00:28:16,020
Choose wisely.

679
00:28:22,690 --> 00:28:24,370
What does this card mean?

680
00:28:25,810 --> 00:28:27,170
This card is the Hermit.

681
00:28:27,890 --> 00:28:30,310
It can also represent an old man.

682
00:28:30,370 --> 00:28:32,420
Does this mean
Danis needs to find a sponsor?

683
00:28:33,950 --> 00:28:36,410
Like, a rich sugar daddy

684
00:28:36,550 --> 00:28:38,690
who can help buy the dorm from Dobby.

685
00:28:38,710 --> 00:28:40,420
Dolly, there you are.

686
00:28:41,530 --> 00:28:42,960
I turned to teach Grandma
how to twerk for a second,

687
00:28:42,980 --> 00:28:43,650
and you vanished.

688
00:28:43,670 --> 00:28:44,710
- Come on, let's go.
- Mom!

689
00:28:44,730 --> 00:28:45,430
- I can't help you.
- Hurry.

690
00:28:45,460 --> 00:28:46,100
Mom, help...

691
00:28:46,120 --> 00:28:46,780
- I can't.
- Don't help him.

692
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:47,960
Help yourself. Come.

693
00:28:49,950 --> 00:28:50,540
Or...

694
00:28:51,660 --> 00:28:53,650
Does Danis actually need a sugar daddy?

695
00:28:53,960 --> 00:28:56,410
How convenient.
I've been wanting to take care of someone.

696
00:28:56,430 --> 00:28:57,530
Take care of yourself first.

697
00:28:58,160 --> 00:28:59,100
You're right.

698
00:28:59,210 --> 00:29:00,170
But I won't allow it!

699
00:29:00,560 --> 00:29:02,490
If she actually gets a sugar daddy,
I can't accept that!

700
00:29:02,510 --> 00:29:03,600
Change it. No more "old man."

701
00:29:03,620 --> 00:29:04,570
Can it be a "young man" instead?!

702
00:29:04,630 --> 00:29:05,510
Ugh!

703
00:29:05,660 --> 00:29:07,710
Let him interpret the cards.

704
00:29:07,830 --> 00:29:09,410
We're getting off track.

705
00:29:09,440 --> 00:29:10,000
Mm.

706
00:29:10,010 --> 00:29:10,730
I won't allow it.

707
00:29:11,180 --> 00:29:11,950
So, Dawin?

708
00:29:12,030 --> 00:29:13,370
This card

709
00:29:13,830 --> 00:29:14,630
means that...

710
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:17,010
an old man will help him change his mind.

711
00:29:20,970 --> 00:29:21,860
I'm sorry,

712
00:29:22,000 --> 00:29:23,660
a fly flew into my mouth.

713
00:29:23,800 --> 00:29:25,740
But that doesn't seem to be the only fly,

714
00:29:25,890 --> 00:29:28,050
since he seems to think
he can fly by deceiving others!

715
00:29:28,640 --> 00:29:29,780
You unhandyman!

716
00:29:30,140 --> 00:29:30,930
How could you say that?

717
00:29:32,330 --> 00:29:32,940
Where are you going?!

718
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:34,050
Come back, come back!

719
00:29:34,060 --> 00:29:35,560
Calm down. Keep reading.

720
00:29:36,070 --> 00:29:37,530
Why come here just to cause trouble?!

721
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:38,740
Take it easy.

722
00:29:39,660 --> 00:29:40,860
Are we gonna get anything out of this?

723
00:29:54,690 --> 00:29:55,320
Who grabbed my butt?!

724
00:29:55,340 --> 00:29:56,450
Who grabbed my butt?!

725
00:29:58,400 --> 00:29:59,650
Yeah, what is it, Dax?

726
00:30:01,130 --> 00:30:02,080
I'm at a hotel.

727
00:30:02,100 --> 00:30:03,820
I... I can't stay in the dorm.

728
00:30:03,870 --> 00:30:04,890
Last night,

729
00:30:05,070 --> 00:30:06,520
Grandpa's ghost haunted me.

730
00:30:06,540 --> 00:30:07,600
This time,

731
00:30:07,890 --> 00:30:09,190
it wasn't Danis.

732
00:30:09,400 --> 00:30:10,530
It was actually him.

733
00:30:10,720 --> 00:30:12,950
If I weren't tied up with
hosting for a shampoo brand,

734
00:30:13,020 --> 00:30:14,650
I would've invited you to Nakhon Sawan.

735
00:30:14,900 --> 00:30:15,560
Huh?

736
00:30:16,180 --> 00:30:16,880
You don't believe me?

737
00:30:16,900 --> 00:30:18,290
Fine. Believe whatever you want!

738
00:30:18,730 --> 00:30:19,540
That's all.

739
00:30:21,510 --> 00:30:23,170
No one believes me
about Grandpa's ghost.

740
00:30:23,590 --> 00:30:25,530
I believe you, though.

741
00:30:25,560 --> 00:30:26,970
Thank you.

742
00:30:30,300 --> 00:30:30,970
Don't come any closer.

743
00:30:31,690 --> 00:30:33,140
Hello, Buddha.

744
00:30:34,700 --> 00:30:37,720
- You're not afraid?
- Stop being scared of me.

745
00:30:38,060 --> 00:30:40,170
I will not do you any harm.

746
00:30:40,190 --> 00:30:43,680
I am here
because I need your help.

747
00:30:43,760 --> 00:30:47,120
You are the only person
who can help me

748
00:30:47,140 --> 00:30:49,170
because you can see me.

749
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:50,740
Why?

750
00:30:50,830 --> 00:30:51,880
What? How would I know?

751
00:30:51,890 --> 00:30:52,880
Huh...

752
00:30:52,890 --> 00:30:54,230
Maybe because...

753
00:30:54,250 --> 00:30:56,130
you are my grandson.

754
00:30:56,140 --> 00:31:00,090
Our bond lets us connect with each other.

755
00:31:00,310 --> 00:31:01,770
- Bond?
- Mm.

756
00:31:01,910 --> 00:31:03,140
I've never seen you

757
00:31:03,150 --> 00:31:04,730
except in your funeral photo.

758
00:31:04,750 --> 00:31:06,970
Well, now you see me.

759
00:31:07,930 --> 00:31:09,650
Have you heard of Big Ass?

760
00:31:09,810 --> 00:31:12,280
♫Is this what's called "destiny"?♫

761
00:31:12,300 --> 00:31:13,830
♫That led our paths♫

762
00:31:13,850 --> 00:31:15,510
♫To cross and make us meet♫

763
00:31:15,530 --> 00:31:16,770
Pick a song, Grandpa.

764
00:31:17,010 --> 00:31:18,420
Maybe it is because...

765
00:31:18,440 --> 00:31:19,730
the heavens

766
00:31:19,740 --> 00:31:23,060
sent you to help me.

767
00:31:23,070 --> 00:31:24,350
Thank heavens.

768
00:31:24,370 --> 00:31:26,450
Dobby, my beloved grandson!

769
00:31:27,930 --> 00:31:28,790
Wait...

770
00:31:29,070 --> 00:31:30,110
You said, "beloved grandson"?

771
00:31:30,710 --> 00:31:32,450
Didn't you cut ties with my mom?

772
00:31:34,310 --> 00:31:36,690
Go away. Go ask someone else!

773
00:31:37,190 --> 00:31:38,080
I'm not helping you!

774
00:31:38,520 --> 00:31:39,370
I'm going to bed,

775
00:31:39,700 --> 00:31:40,500
so don't bother me!

776
00:31:44,980 --> 00:31:47,470
You are just as stubborn as your mom.

777
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:49,720
I will not give up that easily.

778
00:31:49,850 --> 00:31:50,770
What are you mumbling about?

779
00:31:50,790 --> 00:31:52,500
I am talking to myself!

780
00:32:02,570 --> 00:32:04,290
Are you really asleep?

781
00:32:04,760 --> 00:32:06,410
Pretending to be asleep, huh?

782
00:32:06,430 --> 00:32:08,570
It is so obvious.

783
00:32:08,590 --> 00:32:09,930
Go learn how to act.

784
00:32:11,890 --> 00:32:13,840
I know you are not asleep.

785
00:32:13,860 --> 00:32:15,270
Stop pretending.

786
00:32:21,150 --> 00:32:22,610
Bang! Bang!

787
00:32:22,630 --> 00:32:23,940
Bang! Bang!

788
00:32:23,970 --> 00:32:25,360
Bang! Bang!

789
00:32:25,380 --> 00:32:26,440
- Bang! Bang!
- Hey!

790
00:32:26,450 --> 00:32:27,800
Bang! Bang!

791
00:32:28,130 --> 00:32:29,200
Bam, bam, bam, bam.

792
00:32:29,210 --> 00:32:30,820
Bam, bam, bam, bam.

793
00:32:38,990 --> 00:32:42,560
Everybody!!

794
00:32:42,580 --> 00:32:46,200
Put your hands up, hands up in the air!

795
00:32:46,220 --> 00:32:48,650
In the air, put your hands up!

796
00:32:55,370 --> 00:32:57,050
Our shampoo...

797
00:32:57,270 --> 00:33:00,250
You did not
sleep well last night, huh, Dobby?

798
00:33:00,260 --> 00:33:01,370
Research...

799
00:33:02,450 --> 00:33:03,450
shows that

800
00:33:03,460 --> 00:33:06,300
the natural essence

801
00:33:06,320 --> 00:33:07,930
is good for your hair health...

802
00:33:07,950 --> 00:33:09,640
Sell these rattle-rattle drums!

803
00:33:10,100 --> 00:33:13,270
- It helps your hair grow nicely.
- Here are the rattle-rattle drums!

804
00:33:13,300 --> 00:33:16,530
Rattle-rattle drums!

805
00:33:16,550 --> 00:33:17,850
It makes your hair roots

806
00:33:18,390 --> 00:33:19,150
go rattle-rattle.

807
00:33:20,970 --> 00:33:22,870
Um, I meant like...

808
00:33:23,490 --> 00:33:25,640
It makes your rattle-rattle hair roots

809
00:33:25,930 --> 00:33:28,000
go all swish-swish strong!

810
00:33:31,130 --> 00:33:34,200
You are witty. Well done.

811
00:33:35,460 --> 00:33:36,250
Yes.

812
00:33:36,630 --> 00:33:39,000
A great shampoo like this

813
00:33:39,020 --> 00:33:41,570
would never have been made

814
00:33:41,590 --> 00:33:43,290
without Mr. Chanint Panthong's

815
00:33:43,390 --> 00:33:44,710
sharp vision.

816
00:33:47,110 --> 00:33:50,270
Our talented executive has
personally tested this product

817
00:33:50,310 --> 00:33:51,760
and seen the results, yes?

818
00:33:51,780 --> 00:33:52,390
Yes.

819
00:33:52,820 --> 00:33:54,750
Black Shell shampoo is why

820
00:33:54,770 --> 00:33:56,980
his hair is thick, black, and strong.

821
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:58,720
I kind of want to give him a backhand

822
00:33:58,740 --> 00:34:01,330
to see if his hair roots
are actually strong.

823
00:34:05,770 --> 00:34:06,490
Grandpa, don't!

824
00:34:16,469 --> 00:34:17,320
I apologize.

825
00:34:17,340 --> 00:34:18,330
Mr. Chanint, I'm so sorry.

826
00:34:21,810 --> 00:34:22,290
Not that!

827
00:34:22,300 --> 00:34:23,010
Where is it?

828
00:34:23,020 --> 00:34:24,179
I'm sorry, Mr. Chanint.

829
00:34:28,320 --> 00:34:29,880
[The D Dorm]

830
00:34:32,290 --> 00:34:35,050
Now that you've ruined my life,
are you satisfied, Grandpa?

831
00:34:35,070 --> 00:34:37,050
All the organizers canceled my gigs.

832
00:34:37,139 --> 00:34:37,840
You don't believe me?

833
00:34:37,850 --> 00:34:38,610
Look!

834
00:34:38,630 --> 00:34:39,600
[Dobby, you're banned for good]
[The agencies are all banning you]

835
00:34:39,600 --> 00:34:40,300
[If you're banned,
how are you gonna make a living?]

836
00:34:40,770 --> 00:34:43,050
I am sorry. I did not mean to.

837
00:34:45,400 --> 00:34:47,610
Well, I did it on purpose,
but I did not want it to be this bad.

838
00:34:48,889 --> 00:34:51,210
It all started because of you.

839
00:34:51,590 --> 00:34:53,530
You would not help me.

840
00:34:53,550 --> 00:34:54,679
How about this?

841
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:56,780
If you help me,

842
00:34:56,909 --> 00:34:59,210
I will reincarnate

843
00:34:59,730 --> 00:35:02,480
and stop bothering you.

844
00:35:02,530 --> 00:35:05,760
You can sell the dorm or
do whatever you want with it.

845
00:35:08,370 --> 00:35:10,030
So what do you need my help with?

846
00:35:10,560 --> 00:35:11,300
Well...

847
00:35:11,860 --> 00:35:16,220
it happened on the day I bit the dust...

848
00:35:17,260 --> 00:35:20,280
There is one watermelon.

849
00:35:20,470 --> 00:35:23,450
Split it left.

850
00:35:23,760 --> 00:35:26,940
Split it right.

851
00:35:27,240 --> 00:35:29,120
Watermelon.

852
00:35:29,170 --> 00:35:32,070
♫Watermelon, watermelon, watermelon♫

853
00:35:32,090 --> 00:35:34,190
♫Big and sweet treat♫

854
00:35:34,210 --> 00:35:35,260
♫Whoever eats...♫

855
00:35:35,300 --> 00:35:36,090
What?

856
00:35:36,100 --> 00:35:37,400
I was doing Tai Chi.

857
00:35:38,100 --> 00:35:39,570
Why did I suddenly sing mor lam?

858
00:35:46,150 --> 00:35:47,130
Who is that?

859
00:35:59,190 --> 00:36:01,290
Why is Gaysorn's photo here?

860
00:36:05,590 --> 00:36:06,630
Gaysorn!

861
00:36:06,830 --> 00:36:08,830
Gaysorn, wait for me!

862
00:36:09,690 --> 00:36:11,360
Gaysorn!

863
00:36:12,570 --> 00:36:15,130
Where are you running off to, Gaysorn?!

864
00:36:15,340 --> 00:36:17,070
Wait for me!

865
00:36:18,050 --> 00:36:19,270
Gaysorn...

866
00:36:21,550 --> 00:36:23,680
Gaysorn!!

867
00:36:26,980 --> 00:36:28,240
Gaysorn!

868
00:36:29,980 --> 00:36:30,980
Gay...

869
00:36:31,950 --> 00:36:32,950
Gay...

870
00:36:40,680 --> 00:36:42,680
Was my life not tragic?

871
00:36:43,890 --> 00:36:46,630
Gaysorn was my first love.

872
00:36:46,650 --> 00:36:48,480
That day, we both

873
00:36:48,540 --> 00:36:50,910
tried to run away together on the train,

874
00:36:51,270 --> 00:36:54,150
but my dad caught us.

875
00:36:54,950 --> 00:36:58,920
He then forced me to marry
your grandmother.

876
00:36:58,940 --> 00:37:03,550
After that, I never saw Gaysorn again!

877
00:37:09,720 --> 00:37:10,460
Serves you right.

878
00:37:11,790 --> 00:37:13,880
You hate arranged marriages yourself,

879
00:37:13,900 --> 00:37:15,710
but you still forced my mom into one?

880
00:37:15,730 --> 00:37:16,730
One thing to say to you:

881
00:37:16,980 --> 00:37:17,920
"Serves you right."

882
00:37:18,390 --> 00:37:20,610
You would not understand.

883
00:37:20,630 --> 00:37:23,550
It is very complicated.

884
00:37:23,570 --> 00:37:24,540
Huh?

885
00:37:24,610 --> 00:37:26,590
Complicated.

886
00:37:26,610 --> 00:37:28,150
Complicate...

887
00:37:29,200 --> 00:37:29,940
Complex?

888
00:37:29,980 --> 00:37:30,560
Mm.

889
00:37:31,160 --> 00:37:32,290
The thing is...

890
00:37:32,310 --> 00:37:38,490
you need to find out
who owns Gaysorn's picture.

891
00:37:38,510 --> 00:37:41,010
Then take me to them,

892
00:37:41,030 --> 00:37:43,250
so I can find out more about her.

893
00:37:43,270 --> 00:37:46,850
And I will finally be able to apologize to her,
just once in my life.

894
00:37:46,870 --> 00:37:49,010
Wait, Grandpa. Did you forget?

895
00:37:49,740 --> 00:37:50,530
You're a ghost.

896
00:37:51,590 --> 00:37:52,730
Just disappear and go find her!

897
00:37:52,740 --> 00:37:54,110
Why do you need my help?

898
00:37:54,150 --> 00:37:55,970
I have tried that many times already.

899
00:37:55,980 --> 00:37:58,000
It is no use.

900
00:37:58,020 --> 00:38:00,460
I cannot communicate with anyone.

901
00:38:00,490 --> 00:38:04,370
You are the only person
who can help me with this.

902
00:38:06,690 --> 00:38:08,800
If I help you,

903
00:38:09,310 --> 00:38:10,360
you'll stop bothering me, right?

904
00:38:12,060 --> 00:38:13,770
And you'll let me sell this dorm, right?

905
00:38:15,350 --> 00:38:16,690
What?!

906
00:38:16,730 --> 00:38:17,890
Shaking hands?

907
00:38:18,010 --> 00:38:19,640
Here! Fist bump.

908
00:38:19,650 --> 00:38:21,370
That's how Gen Z does it, Grandpa!

909
00:38:21,390 --> 00:38:24,410
I am not a Gen Z. I am a baby boomer.

910
00:38:25,520 --> 00:38:26,450
Fine, I'm in.

911
00:38:27,350 --> 00:38:28,640
Old people are so hard to understand.

912
00:38:30,030 --> 00:38:31,650
Okay, Grandpa, let's go with that.

913
00:38:34,340 --> 00:38:35,400
Gaysorn...

914
00:38:36,050 --> 00:38:37,890
[We're not moving out,
we love this dorm!!]

915
00:38:41,190 --> 00:38:42,810
If we can't talk this out,

916
00:38:42,830 --> 00:38:45,560
I'll have to rally the tenants to protest!

917
00:38:45,600 --> 00:38:46,570
Mm.

918
00:38:46,730 --> 00:38:47,770
I'm done.

919
00:38:49,900 --> 00:38:53,340
"Please show some compassion
for your poor tenants."

920
00:38:55,290 --> 00:38:55,910
What an...

921
00:38:56,070 --> 00:38:59,110
adorable little protest, sweetheart.

922
00:38:59,330 --> 00:39:00,350
I finished mine as well.

923
00:39:00,500 --> 00:39:01,410
Can I see it?

924
00:39:02,180 --> 00:39:03,220
Here.

925
00:39:03,240 --> 00:39:05,330
"First love is hard to move on,

926
00:39:05,350 --> 00:39:07,160
cause I adore the one I gaze upon.

927
00:39:07,180 --> 00:39:09,150
Since it's my first love,

928
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:11,290
stepping away would be too much, love."

929
00:39:12,640 --> 00:39:13,690
There are two meanings to it.

930
00:39:13,710 --> 00:39:14,720
The first one

931
00:39:14,730 --> 00:39:16,260
is the love I have for you, Ms. Danis.

932
00:39:16,280 --> 00:39:17,360
Second,

933
00:39:17,380 --> 00:39:19,610
it's the love that the tenants
have for this dorm.

934
00:39:19,630 --> 00:39:20,820
Guard Dum,

935
00:39:20,840 --> 00:39:22,430
just bring the signs to
Auntie Duang and the others.

936
00:39:22,460 --> 00:39:23,410
They're waiting.

937
00:39:23,450 --> 00:39:25,190
- Oh, alright.
- Thank you.

938
00:39:38,340 --> 00:39:38,870
Hey...

939
00:39:39,380 --> 00:39:40,380
- Hey!
- What? Hey!

940
00:39:40,780 --> 00:39:42,070
Hey, Mr. Dobby.

941
00:39:42,090 --> 00:39:43,100
Why didn't you catch her?

942
00:39:43,150 --> 00:39:43,860
Yeah.

943
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:44,930
Why did I have to?

944
00:39:44,960 --> 00:39:46,250
This isn't a K-drama!

945
00:39:46,270 --> 00:39:48,200
Wow, you're heartless!

946
00:39:48,230 --> 00:39:50,040
Come on, you wrinkled my sleeves.

947
00:39:50,270 --> 00:39:51,430
Hey, wait...

948
00:39:51,450 --> 00:39:53,020
Why did you put up these signs?

949
00:39:53,050 --> 00:39:53,670
What's this?

950
00:39:53,680 --> 00:39:54,930
"Ungrateful grandson."

951
00:39:55,100 --> 00:39:56,290
"We're not leaving."

952
00:39:56,300 --> 00:39:59,130
What? "First love...I love my mom." What?!

953
00:39:59,150 --> 00:40:00,450
Take them all down.

954
00:40:00,550 --> 00:40:01,850
I'm not selling this dorm anymore!

955
00:40:01,870 --> 00:40:02,840
- Huh?!
- Huh?

956
00:40:03,160 --> 00:40:04,810
What? Why did you change your mind?

957
00:40:04,890 --> 00:40:06,470
Well...

958
00:40:06,920 --> 00:40:08,950
my grandpa came to me in a dream

959
00:40:09,260 --> 00:40:10,440
and told me,

960
00:40:10,450 --> 00:40:13,030
"I'm too sinful,
so I can't be reincarnated."

961
00:40:13,050 --> 00:40:15,500
That's why he wants me to keep this dorm.

962
00:40:15,520 --> 00:40:16,710
Let people rent it at a low price

963
00:40:16,880 --> 00:40:17,940
to accumulate merit,

964
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:19,430
so that he'll be sent to heaven.

965
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:20,680
And he won't have to burn in hell.

966
00:40:20,700 --> 00:40:21,700
It's too painful.

967
00:40:22,790 --> 00:40:24,390
He did a lot of evil, that sort of thing.

968
00:40:24,460 --> 00:40:25,490
Nonsense.

969
00:40:26,390 --> 00:40:27,590
How am I sinful?

970
00:40:27,930 --> 00:40:30,530
Dobby, when did I get into your dreams?!

971
00:40:32,700 --> 00:40:34,530
But on one condition:

972
00:40:34,760 --> 00:40:36,090
as long as I'm here,

973
00:40:36,110 --> 00:40:37,380
no one can move out

974
00:40:37,630 --> 00:40:39,250
without my permission.

975
00:40:39,690 --> 00:40:41,060
Why this condition?

976
00:40:41,070 --> 00:40:41,430
Huh?

977
00:40:42,400 --> 00:40:43,830
It's none of your business!

978
00:40:44,240 --> 00:40:45,780
If you don't want me to sell this dorm,

979
00:40:45,820 --> 00:40:46,850
just do as I say.

980
00:40:47,040 --> 00:40:47,860
It's that simple.

981
00:40:48,660 --> 00:40:50,140
Hey, put them all down.

982
00:40:50,740 --> 00:40:52,380
"First love is hard to move...
Oh, what the heck?"

983
00:40:52,410 --> 00:40:53,620
What sin did I commit?

984
00:40:54,370 --> 00:40:55,570
How am I sinful?!

985
00:40:55,840 --> 00:40:56,490
Dobby!

986
00:40:57,100 --> 00:40:59,230
Talk to me. How am I sinful?!

987
00:41:00,600 --> 00:41:01,880
It's alright, Ms. Danis,

988
00:41:02,550 --> 00:41:04,430
at least he's not going to
sell this dorm.

989
00:41:05,490 --> 00:41:08,050
If we follow his rules,
everything should be fine.

990
00:41:09,070 --> 00:41:10,750
I still can't trust him.

991
00:41:11,060 --> 00:41:12,690
There's gotta be some reason behind this.

992
00:41:12,870 --> 00:41:13,790
I don't know...

993
00:41:14,010 --> 00:41:16,970
Perhaps the old man Dawin mentioned
is his grandpa?

994
00:41:17,770 --> 00:41:18,730
Hmph...

995
00:41:22,890 --> 00:41:24,320
Was that good enough for you, Grandpa?

996
00:41:24,950 --> 00:41:26,550
Don't forget your promise.

997
00:41:26,570 --> 00:41:28,050
I will not forget.

998
00:41:28,360 --> 00:41:30,270
As soon as I meet Gaysorn,

999
00:41:30,290 --> 00:41:31,580
I will be reborn right away.

1000
00:41:31,590 --> 00:41:33,570
I will not bother you ever again.

1001
00:41:33,590 --> 00:41:34,530
Deal.

1002
00:41:42,830 --> 00:41:44,690
Ugh! Leave it.

1003
00:41:44,700 --> 00:41:46,190
It's a deal, Grandpa.

1004
00:42:00,070 --> 00:42:00,990
Why are you smiling?

1005
00:42:03,410 --> 00:42:04,750
I am happy.

1006
00:42:05,530 --> 00:42:07,530
I have not seen Gaysorn in a long time.

1007
00:42:07,650 --> 00:42:08,830
If I get to see her again...

1008
00:42:10,250 --> 00:42:12,470
it would be nice
to apologize to her at least once

1009
00:42:12,490 --> 00:42:14,590
before I go.

1010
00:42:22,850 --> 00:42:23,850
Have you ever...

1011
00:42:24,790 --> 00:42:26,290
wanted to apologize to Mom like this?

1012
00:42:31,860 --> 00:42:33,240
I did not do anything wrong!

1013
00:42:33,960 --> 00:42:35,920
Your mom was the one at fault!

1014
00:42:40,510 --> 00:42:42,200
It's no use talking to someone like you.

1015
00:43:11,810 --> 00:43:13,340
Mommy...

1016
00:43:13,350 --> 00:43:16,500
Today, my teacher asked
me to draw a family picture.

1017
00:43:16,520 --> 00:43:19,390
Why are there only
three people in our family?

1018
00:43:19,410 --> 00:43:23,730
Why don't we have
a Grandpa and Grandma like other families?

1019
00:43:27,340 --> 00:43:30,050
Why are you crying, Mommy?

1020
00:43:55,950 --> 00:43:56,950
Finally...

1021
00:43:58,530 --> 00:43:59,970
I get to meet you,

1022
00:44:00,810 --> 00:44:01,730
Dobby.

1023
00:44:14,110 --> 00:44:18,520
[Nakhon Sawan, 2004]

1024
00:44:18,540 --> 00:44:19,750
Here to see your grandchild or child?

1025
00:44:19,770 --> 00:44:21,820
Oh, my grandson.

1026
00:44:22,580 --> 00:44:24,090
His name is Dobby.

1027
00:44:24,170 --> 00:44:25,510
- Dobby?
- Yeah.

1028
00:44:25,950 --> 00:44:28,350
His mother probably likes
'Harry Potter,' huh?

1029
00:44:29,310 --> 00:44:31,830
Dobby. What an odd name.

1030
00:44:32,350 --> 00:44:35,680
Why didn't she name him "Song" or "Gui"?

1031
00:44:35,690 --> 00:44:36,770
They sound prettier.

1032
00:44:38,530 --> 00:44:39,340
There.

1033
00:44:39,740 --> 00:44:42,930
The boy sitting alone
with a sock on his hand.

1034
00:44:45,080 --> 00:44:45,760
So?

1035
00:44:46,470 --> 00:44:47,850
He's handsome, just like me, yeah?

1036
00:44:49,370 --> 00:44:50,880
I'll take a photo.

1037
00:44:54,220 --> 00:44:56,530
Why don't you get closer to take a photo?

1038
00:45:00,130 --> 00:45:02,300
It's fine. I can take it from here.

1039
00:45:22,290 --> 00:45:22,970
Hey!

1040
00:45:23,370 --> 00:45:24,580
Don't peek, Grandpa!

1041
00:45:24,710 --> 00:45:25,770
Peek...

1042
00:45:27,770 --> 00:45:31,040
When I was younger,
I had a much more defined six-pack.

1043
00:45:44,650 --> 00:45:46,400
I want you to be my sidekick

1044
00:45:46,420 --> 00:45:47,920
and help me find Grandma Gaysorn.

1045
00:45:47,990 --> 00:45:49,020
What do I have to do?

1046
00:45:49,040 --> 00:45:50,450
There is only one way.

1047
00:45:50,700 --> 00:45:51,240
Hm?

1048
00:45:51,300 --> 00:45:53,570
Just get Danis on your side.

1049
00:45:53,590 --> 00:45:54,950
Everything will be easier.

1050
00:45:54,970 --> 00:45:56,800
Danis hates my guts.

1051
00:45:56,900 --> 00:45:58,090
Why would she help me?!

1052
00:46:00,200 --> 00:46:01,840
What would you like me
to tell you about your fortune?

1053
00:46:01,960 --> 00:46:04,300
I want to know
if the coffee shop owner downstairs

1054
00:46:04,330 --> 00:46:06,080
is a good match for me.

1055
00:46:06,470 --> 00:46:08,080
His shop is about to open,
but I've never even seen him.

1056
00:46:16,990 --> 00:46:20,290
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1057
00:46:20,310 --> 00:46:24,370
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

1058
00:46:26,840 --> 00:46:32,280
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

1059
00:46:34,000 --> 00:46:38,770
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

1060
00:46:41,120 --> 00:46:47,370
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

1061
00:46:48,240 --> 00:46:52,800
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

1062
00:46:52,830 --> 00:46:56,340
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

1063
00:46:56,360 --> 00:46:59,980
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

1064
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:03,500
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

1065
00:47:03,520 --> 00:47:06,110
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

1066
00:47:06,130 --> 00:47:12,720
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

1067
00:47:12,990 --> 00:47:19,800
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

1068
00:47:20,080 --> 00:47:27,290
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

1069
00:47:27,310 --> 00:47:34,350
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

1070
00:47:34,410 --> 00:47:37,450
[The D Dorm]
